# Default: normalise everything to LF in the repository.
# This must come FIRST — in .gitattributes the *last* matching pattern wins, so
# a catch-all placed below would silently override the specific rules under it.
* text=auto

# Windows scripts must keep CRLF *in the committed blob*, not merely on
# checkout. `install-my-daemon.bat` is downloaded straight from GitHub raw,
# which serves the stored bytes and never applies git's checkout conversion —
# so a repo that stores LF ships an LF batch file to every user who downloads
# the installer.
#
# cmd.exe tolerates LF in simple scripts but not reliably in the two constructs
# these files lean on: parenthesised `if (...)` blocks and `set /p`.
#
# `-text`, NOT `text eol=crlf`. The latter stores LF in the repository and only
# converts on checkout, which does nothing for a file fetched over raw HTTP.
# `-text` disables conversion entirely, so the CRLF bytes are what gets stored
# and therefore what gets served. `diff` keeps them readable in patches.
*.bat -text diff
*.cmd -text diff
*.vbs -text diff
